athena-branding (1.2.0) thor; urgency=low

  * Ship target-system GRUB background image.  Observed 2026-05-22
    on a fresh end-to-end install: GRUB on the installed target had
    our distributor string ("Asgard GNU/Linux" menu entries via
    1.1.0's GRUB_DISTRIBUTOR override) but no graphical background —
    stock Debian's GRUB background ships from desktop-base, which we
    displace via Provides+Conflicts+Replaces.  Displacing without
    replacing left the background gap.

  * data/50-athena.cfg now also sets
        GRUB_BACKGROUND=/usr/share/athena-branding/grub-background.png
    so /etc/grub.d/05_debian_theme's GRUB_BACKGROUND pickup paints
    the boot menu with our Aegis splash.

  * debian/rules grew a third rsvg-convert call rendering
    data/aegis-dark.svg → _build/png/grub-background.png at 1920x1080
    (the dark variant keeps menu text readable against the midnight
    sky; GRUB scales to lower-res monitors automatically).

  * debian/install ships _build/png/grub-background.png to
    /usr/share/athena-branding/.

  * debian/postinst (new) re-runs update-grub on configure so the
    GRUB_DISTRIBUTOR + GRUB_BACKGROUND from 50-athena.cfg land in
    /boot/grub/grub.cfg even when athena-branding installs AFTER
    grub-pc/grub-efi-amd64 (the typical pkgsel/tasksel order — by
    the time we configure, grub's own postinst-driven update-grub
    has already run without seeing our 50-athena.cfg).  No-op when
    update-grub isn't on PATH (live ISO / chroot without grub).
    `|| true` on the update-grub call so transient warnings don't
    block install completion.

  * Pattern source: docs/branding-methodology.md § 5 catalogue —
    runtime-system GRUB background follows the same Pattern B
    drop-in-static-asset shape as the GNOME wallpaper.  Companion
    to the installer-ISO GRUB splash shipped in COMP-01f Phase 2.

 -- Athena Linux <athena@local>  Thu, 22 May 2026 08:00:00 +0000

athena-branding (1.1.0) thor; urgency=low

  * Displace upstream desktop-base via Provides/Conflicts/Replaces.
    task-desktop's hard Depends on desktop-base previously dragged
    Debian's branded wallpapers, plymouth theme, GRUB theme, emblem
    icons, and a competing gschema override onto the installed
    system; that closure is now blocked.
  * Ship /usr/share/pixmaps/asgard.svg — distributor logo, gold Α
    on a midnight disc, geometric anchor identical to the Aegis
    wallpaper.  Read by gnome-control-center's About panel and
    the user-account panel via /etc/os-release LOGO=asgard
    (set by athena-base-files).
  * Ship /etc/default/grub.d/50-athena.cfg setting
    GRUB_DISTRIBUTOR="Asgard" so update-grub on the installed
    system emits "Asgard GNU/Linux" menu entries instead of the
    lsb_release-fallback literal "Debian".

 -- Athena Linux <athena@local>  Wed, 21 May 2026 17:00:00 +0000

athena-branding (1.0.0) thor; urgency=low

  * Initial release (FORK-01 Step 7, deb-half).
    - Ships default GNOME wallpaper "Aegis" (light + dark) under
      /usr/share/backgrounds/athena/, both SVG and 3840×2160 PNG.
    - gsettings schema override sets aegis-light/dark as the default
      desktop & lock-screen wallpaper for new users.
    - gnome-background-properties XML registers the wallpaper pair
      in the GNOME Settings → Background picker.
  * The udeb half (athena-branding-installer, debconf-overrides for
    installer chrome) is intentionally deferred to a follow-up
    release pending user approval — see docs/plans/fork-source.md
    § "Step 7" and the DEF-2 note for the broader desktop-base
    replacement scope.

 -- Athena Linux <athena@local>  Wed, 21 May 2026 13:00:00 +0000
